{"chunk_id": "eb8bed1c1234", "text": "In this section Sanjaya describes the ferocious duel between Bhima and Karna during the Kurukshetra war. Bhima first slays several of Dhritarashtra\u2019s sons with single arrows, provoking Karna to confront him in grief and fury. The two heroes exchange devastating showers of arrows, compared repeatedly to storms, beasts, and cosmic forces. Duryodhana sends seven more brothers to rescue Karna, but Bhima kills them all, fulfilling part of his terrible vow. He briefly mourns Vikarna, the one Kaurava brother who had once spoken justly for the Pandavas, showing the tragic complexity of the war. Bhima\u2019s roar signals victory to Yudhishthira, while Duryodhana realizes too late that Vidura\u2019s earlier warnings about injustice and the dice game are now bearing their deadly consequences.\nBhima and Karna wage a ferocious duel; Bhima slays several of Duryodhana\u2019s brothers including Vikarna, fulfilling his vow and shaking the Kaurava army.\nThemes: Bhima\u2013Karna duel, vengeance and vows, fratricidal loss, fate and consequences, battle carnage", "vector": [-0.010856052860617638, -0.016181036829948425, -0.0077049387618899345, 0.009440045803785324, -0.014027110300958157, 0.02655179053544998, -0.02414524368941784, 0.0005787845002487302, -0.02066173404455185, -0.033611882477998734, 0.005421378184109926, 0.014532351866364479, 0.014186659827828407, 0.005138841923326254, 0.0007503839442506433, 0.001593007706105709, 0.040951184928417206, 0.0028536194004118443, 0.03326619043946266, -0.025740744546055794, -0.00974585022777319, -0.0020724888890981674, -0.0006315523642115295, 0.03440963104367256, -0.03342574089765549, 0.028133995831012726, 0.015463060699403286, -0.028772195801138878, 0.006893892772495747, -0.00914753694087267, -0.01251803245395422, -0.01603478193283081, 0.0072661759331822395, -0.002642547944560647, -0.0253019817173481, 0.019877279177308083, -0.003179367631673813, -0.015569427981972694, 0.011740226298570633, -0.000339043